    "stem": "Kabir must divide ₹$120$ among three friends in the ratio $3 : 4 : 5$.\n\nWhich statements correctly give the three shares?",
    "item_type": "three_statement",
    "options": {
      "A": "1 and 2 only",
      "B": "1 and 3 only",
      "C": "2 and 3 only",
      "D": "1, 2 and 3"
    },
    "statements": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "text": "Add the terms $3+4+5=12$, then give $\\frac{3}{12}\\times 120$, $\\frac{4}{12}\\times 120$, and $\\frac{5}{12}\\times 120$, so ₹$30$, ₹$40$, and ₹$50$."
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "text": "Each share is the whole ₹$120$ times that friend’s ratio term divided by the sum of all terms."
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "text": "Divide $120$ by each of $3$, $4$, and $5$ separately, getting $40$, $30$, and $24$."
      }
    ],
